{"id": "sevt_01L59j1jV7YXUuBE7VfTTRyo", "content": [{"text": "**Evidence**\n- Cart deployed `df06e76` at 14:43:20. Cart p99 went from about 75 ms at 14:42 to 3,730 ms at 14:43 and stayed at 3.5\u20134.6 s. The checkout deploy (14:41) and auth deploy (14:44:50) don't fit the timing. The jump starts before the auth deploy, and checkout was clean for two minutes after its own deploy.\n- The diff replaces one batched `sku_id IN (...)` query with a per-cart-line `SkuPrice.objects.filter(sku_id=...)` inside a loop. That is an N+1 query pattern, so each cart pricing call now makes one query per line.\n- The log shows 1,888 single-SKU `WHERE sku_id = ?` queries. Before the deploy, cart only issued the batched `IN (?)` form.\n- I did not check `db_pool_utilization` or the per-query durations after the deploy.\n\n**Root cause:** `df06e76` \u2014 it changed cart pricing from one batched SKU query to one query per cart line (N+1), which multiplies the DB round-trips for every pricing call. Reverting it should bring p99 back down.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:51:37.148849Z", "type": "agent.message"}
